## CDN Stack — VLESS over WebSocket

Traffic is disguised as normal HTTPS and routed through Cloudflare's CDN. This
lets the proxy survive on networks that block direct server IPs, because
Cloudflare's edge addresses are broadly trusted and expensive to block wholesale.

The `cdn-proxy` Nginx container terminates TLS on port {{NGINX_HTTPS_PORT}} and
forwards WebSocket upgrade requests to the `vless-cdn` Xray backend. Cloudflare
should be configured in **proxy mode** (orange cloud) for this domain so traffic
flows through Cloudflare's edge, not directly to the server.

{{CDN_STD_HEADING}}| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Domain | `{{CDN_DOMAIN}}` |
| Port | `{{NGINX_HTTPS_PORT}}` |
| Network | WebSocket (`ws`) |
| Path | `/ws` |
| TLS | enabled |
| Protocol | VLESS |
| UUIDs | `{{VLESS_WS_IDS}}` |

{{CDN_WARP_SECTION}}### TLS (inside container paths)

| | Path |
|--|------|
| Certificate | `{{TLS_CERT_CDN}}` |
| Private key | `{{TLS_KEY_CDN}}` |

